\f1\b\fs28 \cf2 Section 1: General Awareness (Questions 1\'9630)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf2 1. Which carnivorous plant catches insects by snapping its modified leaf lobes shut in less than a second?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Pitcher plant\
\
(B) Venus flytrap\
\
(C) Sundew\
\
(D) Rafflesia\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Venus flytrap.
\f0\b0  Rapid turgor pressure changes trigger the sensitive trigger hairs to snap shut.\
\

\f1\b 2. Which flightless bird native to New Zealand has nostrils located at the tip of its long bill to sniff out insects underground?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Emu\
\
(B) Ostrich\
\
(C) Kiwi\
\
(D) Penguin\
\

\f1\b Answer: (C) Kiwi.
\f0\b0  It is one of the few birds that relies heavily on smell rather than sight to hunt.\
\

\f1\b 3. The periodic shedding of outer skin, feathers, or exoskeletons to facilitate new growth is known as:
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Hibernation\
\
(B) Moulting\
\
(C) Camouflage\
\
(D) Metamorphosis\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Moulting.
\f0\b0  Seen commonly in reptiles, insects, and birds.\
\

\f1\b 4. Plants that grow on other trees purely for physical support without drawing nutrients or causing harm are called:
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Parasites\
\
(B) Epiphytes\
\
(C) Saprophytes\
\
(D) Xerophytes\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Epiphytes.
\f0\b0  Many tropical orchids and ferns are classic examples.\
\

\f1\b 5. Which layer of Earth's atmosphere contains the vital ozone layer that absorbs harmful UV rays?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Troposphere\
\
(B) Stratosphere\
\
(C) Mesosphere\
\
(D) Thermosphere\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Stratosphere.
\f0\b0  It sits directly above the troposphere.\
\

\f1\b 6. What is the line dividing the illuminated day side from the dark night side of a planetary body called?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Prime Meridian\
\
(B) Terminator line\
\
(C) Horizon\
\
(D) Tropic of Cancer\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Terminator line.
\f0\b0  Also known as the "twilight zone."\
\

\f1\b 7. Which is the world's largest hot desert?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Gobi Desert\
\
(B) Kalahari Desert\
\
(C) Sahara Desert\
\
(D) Thar Desert\
\

\f1\b Answer: (C) Sahara Desert.
\f0\b0  (Antarctica is the largest desert overall, but Sahara is the largest 
\f2\i hot
\f0\i0  desert).\
\

\f1\b 8. What term describes the progressive increase in the concentration of toxins (like microplastics or heavy metals) at higher levels of the food chain?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Eutrophication\
\
(B) Biomagnification\
\
(C) Desertification\
\
(D) Decomposition\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Biomagnification.
\f0\b0  Apex predators accumulate the highest concentrations.\
\

\f1\b 9. Which planet in our solar system is known as the "Morning Star" or "Evening Star" due to its exceptional brightness?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Mars\
\
(B) Venus\
\
(C) Jupiter\
\
(D) Mercury\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Venus.
\f0\b0  Its thick cloud cover reflects sunlight strongly (high albedo).\
\

\f1\b 10. Which mineral is indispensable for the production of hemoglobin in human red blood cells?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Calcium\
\
(B) Iron\
\
(C) Iodine\
\
(D) Zinc\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Iron.
\f0\b0  A deficiency causes nutritional anemia.\
\

\f1\b 11. Who invented the World Wide Web (WWW) at CERN in 1989?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Tim Berners-Lee\
\
(B) Alan Turing\
\
(C) Bill Gates\
\
(D) Charles Babbage\
\

\f1\b Answer: (A) Tim Berners-Lee.
\f0\b0 \
\

\f1\b 12. Ganymede, the largest natural satellite (moon) in the Solar System, orbits which planet?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Saturn\
\
(B) Jupiter\
\
(C) Uranus\
\
(D) Neptune\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Jupiter.
\f0\b0  Ganymede is even larger than the planet Mercury.\
\

\f1\b 13. Which meteorological instrument measures atmospheric pressure?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Anemometer\
\
(B) Barometer\
\
(C) Hygrometer\
\
(D) Seismograph\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Barometer.
\f0\b0  Anemometers measure wind speed; hygrometers measure humidity.\
\

\f1\b 14. Which narrow body of water separates the southeastern tip of India from Sri Lanka?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Strait of Malacca\
\
(B) Palk Strait\
\
(C) Bering Strait\
\
(D) Strait of Gibraltar\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Palk Strait.
\f0\b0 \
\

\f1\b 15. What is the official currency of Japan?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Yuan\
\
(B) Won\
\
(C) Yen\
\
(D) Ringgit\
\

\f1\b Answer: (C) Yen.
\f0\b0  (Yuan belongs to China; Won to South Korea).\
\

\f1\b 16. Which leader is celebrated as the "Iron Man of India" for integrating hundreds of princely states into the Indian Union?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel\
\
(B) Subhas Chandra Bose\
\
(C) Dr. B.R. Ambedkar\
\
(D) Bhagat Singh\
\

\f1\b Answer: (A) Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel.
\f0\b0 \
\

\f1\b 17. In which city is the headquarters of UNESCO (United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization) located?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Geneva\
\
(B) Paris\
\
(C) New York\
\
(D) Rome\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Paris, France.
\f0\b0 \
\

\f1\b 18. Which is the longest continental mountain range above sea level on Earth?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Himalayas\
\
(B) Rocky Mountains\
\
(C) Andes\
\
(D) Alps\
\

\f1\b Answer: (C) Andes.
\f0\b0  Spanning over 7,000 km along western South America.\
\

\f1\b 19. Which pre-Columbian civilization constructed the mountain citadel of Machu Picchu?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Maya\
\
(B) Aztec\
\
(C) Inca\
\
(D) Olmec\
\

\f1\b Answer: (C) Inca.
\f0\b0  Located in modern-day Peru.\
\

\f1\b 20. Who served as the Chairman of the Drafting Committee of the Indian Constitution?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Dr. Rajendra Prasad\
\
(B) Dr. B.R. Ambedkar\
\
(C) Jawaharlal Nehru\
\
(D) Sarojini Naidu\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Dr. B.R. Ambedkar.
\f0\b0  (Dr. Rajendra Prasad was President of the Constituent Assembly).\
\

\f1\b 21. Which country is commonly referred to as the "Land of the Midnight Sun"?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Norway\
\
(B) Finland\
\
(C) Japan\
\
(D) Iceland\
\

\f1\b Answer: (A) Norway.
\f0\b0  Due to its location within the Arctic Circle where the sun stays above the horizon in summer.\
\

\f1\b 22. Who is the author of the classic fantasy book series 
\f3\i The Chronicles of Narnia
\f1\i0 ?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) J.K. Rowling\
\
(B) C.S. Lewis\
\
(C) Roald Dahl\
\
(D) J.R.R. Tolkien\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) C.S. Lewis.
\f0\b0 \
\

\f1\b 23. What does the common idiom "to burn the midnight oil" mean?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) To waste fuel needlessly\
\
(B) To work or study late into the night\
\
(C) To create chaos deliberately\
\
(D) To wake up early at dawn\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) To work or study late into the night.
\f0\b0 \
\

\f1\b 24. Which Indian author was awarded the 1997 Booker Prize for the novel 
\f3\i The God of Small Things
\f1\i0 ?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Arundhati Roy\
\
(B) Jhumpa Lahiri\
\
(C) Anita Desai\
\
(D) Salman Rushdie\
\

\f1\b Answer: (A) Arundhati Roy.
\f0\b0 \
\

\f1\b 25. In the sport of badminton, what is the feathered or plastic projectile called?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Puck\
\
(B) Shuttlecock\
\
(C) Birdie-disc\
\
(D) Striker\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Shuttlecock.
\f0\b0 \
\

\f1\b 26. Which country hosted the 2024 Summer Olympic Games?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Japan\
\
(B) France\
\
(C) United States\
\
(D) Australia\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) France (Paris).
\f0\b0 \
\

\f1\b 27. The term "Grand Slam" is most prominently associated with which two sports?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Cricket and Hockey\
\
(B) Tennis and Golf\
\
(C) Badminton and Squash\
\
(D) Football and Basketball\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Tennis and Golf.
\f0\b0 \
\

\f1\b 28. The Oscars, presented annually by the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences, recognize achievements in which field?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Cinema / Filmmaking\
\
(B) Television Broadcasting\
\
(C) Recorded Music\
\
(D) Broadway Theatre\
\

\f1\b Answer: (A) Cinema / Filmmaking.
\f0\b0  (Grammys honor music; Emmys honor television).\
\

\f1\b 29. Logical Reasoning: If South-West becomes North, and North-West becomes East, what will West become?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) North-East\
\
(B) South-East\
\
(C) South\
\
(D) North\
\

\f1\b Answer: (A) North-East.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  The rotation is 135\'b0 clockwise (SW + 135\'b0 = North; NW + 135\'b0 = East). Rotating West (270\'b0) by 135\'b0 clockwise yields 45\'b0, which is North-East.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 30. Number Series: Find the missing term: 3, 7, 15, 31, 63, ___?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) 95\
\
(B) 125\
\
(C) 127\
\
(D) 129\
\

\f1\b Answer: (C) 127.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  Each term follows $(n \\times 2) + 1$, or successive additions of double increments ($+4, +8, +16, +32, +64$). $63 + 64 = 127$.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\li4320\fi-4320\ri4320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf2 Section 2: Current Affairs & Global Developments (Questions 31\'9640)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf2 31. India became the first country to land a spacecraft near the lunar south pole with which mission?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Mangalyaan\
\
(B) Chandrayaan-3\
\
(C) Aditya-L1\
\
(D) Gaganyaan\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Chandrayaan-3.
\f0\b0  Its lander, Vikram, touched down on August 23, celebrated as National Space Day in India.\
\

\f1\b 32. Which Nordic country officially became the 32nd member of the NATO alliance in 2024?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Finland\
\
(B) Sweden\
\
(C) Ukraine\
\
(D) Austria\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Sweden.
\f0\b0  (Finland became the 31st member in 2023).\
\

\f1\b 33. Which country won the ICC Men's T20 World Cup title in June 2024?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) South Africa\
\
(B) India\
\
(C) Australia\
\
(D) England\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) India.
\f0\b0  India defeated South Africa in the final in Bridgetown, Barbados.\
\

\f1\b 34. What is the name of ISRO's first dedicated solar observatory mission, placed around the Sun-Earth L1 point?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Astrosat\
\
(B) Aditya-L1\
\
(C) XPoSat\
\
(D) Shukrayaan\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Aditya-L1.
\f0\b0 \
\

\f1\b 35. The 2026 Winter Olympic Games will be hosted by which country?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Italy\
\
(B) France\
\
(C) Canada\
\
(D) Switzerland\
\

\f1\b Answer: (A) Italy (Milano Cortina 2026).
\f0\b0 \
\

\f1\b 36. The 2024 Nobel Peace Prize was awarded to which organization for its efforts toward a nuclear-weapon-free world?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) International Red Cross\
\
(B) Nihon Hidankyo\
\
(C) World Food Programme\
\
(D) Amnesty International\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Nihon Hidankyo.
\f0\b0  A Japanese grassroots organization formed by atomic bomb survivors (Hibakusha).\
\

\f1\b 37. Author Han Kang won the 2024 Nobel Prize in Literature, making her the first writer from which country to win this award?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Japan\
\
(B) South Korea\
\
(C) China\
\
(D) Vietnam\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) South Korea.
\f0\b0 \
\

\f1\b 38. Which city has been selected to host the Summer Olympic Games in 2028?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Brisbane\
\
(B) Los Angeles\
\
(C) London\
\
(D) Doha\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Los Angeles, USA.
\f0\b0 \
\

\f1\b 39. NASA's flagship lunar program aimed at landing astronauts, including the first woman and person of color, back on the Moon is named:
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Apollo\
\
(B) Artemis\
\
(C) Curiosity\
\
(D) New Horizons\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Artemis.
\f0\b0 \
\

\f1\b 40. In which state/union territory is the world's highest railway arch bridge, the Chenab Bridge, located?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Himachal Pradesh\
\
(B) Jammu and Kashmir\
\
(C) Uttarakhand\
\
(D) Sikkim\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Jammu and Kashmir.
\f0\b0  It stands 359 meters above the riverbed, taller than the Eiffel Tower.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\li4320\fi-4320\ri4320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf2 Section 3: Life Skills & Values (Questions 41\'9645)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf2 41. During a group project, a member proposes a concept completely different from yours. What is the most constructive action?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Overrule them immediately and insist on your approach\
\
(B) Listen patiently, evaluate the merits of their idea, and find a way to combine both perspectives\
\
(C) Withdraw from the group and complain to the teacher\
\
(D) Ignore the member and complete the project alone\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B).
\f0\b0  Demonstrates collaborative problem solving, active listening, and open-mindedness.\
\

\f1\b 42. What is "phishing" in the context of cyber safety?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Playing virtual fishing games online\
\
(B) Deceptive messages or emails designed to steal passwords, financial details, or personal data\
\
(C) Updating your computer's firewall software\
\
(D) Browsing educational websites with parent supervision\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B).
\f0\b0  Phishing attempts mimic trusted services to trick users.\
\

\f1\b 43. If an alarming, unverified message about an impending emergency is forwarded in a chat group, what is the right digital response?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Immediately forward it to all your contacts to warn them\
\
(B) Cross-check with credible news outlets or official school authorities before sharing\
\
(C) Retweet and post it on public forums\
\
(D) Panic and leave all groups\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B).
\f0\b0  Stopping the spread of fake news is a core digital literacy skill.\
\

\f1\b 44. What is the healthiest way to manage acute exam stress and cognitive fatigue?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Pulling all-nighters and skipping breakfast\
\
(B) Planning study intervals with the Pomodoro technique, sleeping 8 hours, and practicing deep breathing\
\
(C) Quitting revision entirely\
\
(D) Relying on energy drinks and sugary snacks\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B).
\f0\b0  Structured rest and predictable scheduling protect memory consolidation and reduce anxiety.\
\

\f1\b 45. What is the core definition of "empathy"?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Feeling pity from a superior position\
\
(B) Understanding and sharing the feelings and perspectives of another person\
\
(C) Agreeing with someone even when they are wrong\
\
(D) Offering advice before hearing someone out\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B).
\f0\b0  Empathy involves emotionally and cognitively understanding another's lived experience.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\li4320\fi-4320\ri4320\partightenfactor0

