\f1\b 47. Read the following statements regarding World Heritage Sites and identify which statement(s) are correct:
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Great Barrier Reef is situated off the north-eastern coast of Australia.\uc0\u8232 \
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Taj Mahal was commissioned by the Mughal Emperor Akbar.\uc0\u8232 \
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Mount Everest lies on the border between Nepal and the Tibet Autonomous Region of China.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 (A) 1 and 2 only\u8232 \u8232 (B) 2 and 3 only\u8232 \u8232 (C) 1 and 3 only\u8232 \u8232 (D) 1, 2, and 3\u8232 \u8232 
\f1\b Answer: (C) 1 and 3 only.
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 \u8232 
\f2\i Explanation:
\f0\i0  Statement 2 is incorrect because the Taj Mahal was commissioned by Mughal Emperor Shah Jahan, not Akbar.\uc0\u8232 \
